From a8a4753329be2c37214ea496a93b5ae40b5aa5c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Grinberg <igrinberg@habana.ai>
Date: Sun, 02 Jun 2019 11:40:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] [SW-4185] gaudi: pll: add hbw clk sw glitch w/a

Since the clock switch has a glitch while switching between clocks
different by a factor of about 10, we W/A the problem by performing
the switch in a "gated" manner. That is, we gate the clock output,
perform the switch, and then ungate the clock output.
This way we are able to W/A the clock switch glitch as we wait enough
time for the clock to stabilize before ungating.

Change-Id: I1e455df5e923d549b65ce8ee74884da26dee430a
Signed-off-by: Igor Grinberg <igrinberg@habana.ai>
---

diff --git a/common/pll.c b/common/pll.c
index 81f2065..3e96b9d 100644
--- a/common/pll.c
+++ b/common/pll.c
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@
 	return regmap_readl(pll_base + HL_PLL_DIV_SEL + offset);
 }
 
-static inline void hl_pll_udelay(unsigned int usec)
+void hl_pll_udelay(unsigned int usec)
 {
 	u64 cnt = (cycles_per_usec * usec) / MIN_CYCLES_PER_ITER;
 
